From 6d016961b1910cf3bbc00fb91fcfa663ae66ce89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:05:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] efr32bg22: persistent flash image, IDAU, guest memory
 writes and reset handshake; Python peripheral models

- flash=<image> machine property; flash survives system reset (MSC model
  writes it through the bridge reply)
- external secure attribution unit per AN1374 section 3.3
- bridge reply carries guest memory writes and a reset request; reset
  notification (op 3) lets the server rebuild its peripherals
- tools/efr32bg22: server, models (clocks, EMU, DCDC, TRNG with the SDK
  conditioning self-test, I2C master + PCF8575, GPIO, TIMER, MSC) and a
  generator for register tables/IRQ numbers from the SDK headers

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PdMVRPYdkoKYyoN2UWrcnz
